Good harnesses mix guides and sensors, and use both computational and inferential controls.

4. HARNESS SURFACES
Surface                 Purpose / examples
Context engineering     retrieve, filter, rank, trim, and assemble relevant information
Tool layer              expose safe, well-defined tools and APIs with clear schemas and usage contracts
Execution environment   run actions in isolated, reproducible, and permission-bounded environments
Working state           track current plan, open tasks, intermediate results, and in-flight artifacts
Durable memory          persist summaries, checkpoints, decisions, and long-term facts outside the prompt
Guardrails / permissions enforce policy, least privilege, approval gates, and action boundaries
Observability           log traces, tool calls, costs, errors, screenshots, and runtime metadata
Evals                   automated checks for correctness, safety, quality, and task-specific success
Outputs                 deliver structured artifacts such as answers, code changes, reports, or handoffs

